\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 Sacrificial Elvis
\f0\b0\fs24 \
\pard\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\pardeftab720\fi360\sl264\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f3\fs26 Agent Jones, the only agent to survive the raid on the bio-weapons bunker, sat opposite Director Harding and listened. Covert agents were a suspicious lot and he figured his remarkable survival would be the subject of a great deal of scrutiny from his punctilious boss.\
\'93How is it, Agent Jones, that you are the only one to survive? How is it, that you ended up 100 metres away in a pool of excrement?\'94 Director Hardman had gone over it in his head, again and again, it did not make sense.\
\'93I have no memory of what happened after I entered the bunker, but I can\'92t imagine being covered in shit was by choice. I woke up in a med-facility, with three nurses hosing me down.\'94 The shit bit was true, but the medical staff at the Elvi Infirmary were professional and had cleansed him down with great care. \'93I was told where I was found, but I have no idea how I got there.\'94 He crossed his fingers and prayed to the Dawkins that Hardman would swallow his lie. 
\f4\i The Dawkins? Man, I have been hanging with the Elvi far too much.
\f3\i0 \
\'93I find it difficult to believe electro-pulse grenades caused such a peculiar pattern of destruction. According to the reports, it undermined a path beneath several buildings and blew out the side of a deep excavation in a vacant lot. To top it all off we are being sued by the lease holder. He wants the cost of the clean-up to come from us! That will be coming out of your pay, Agent Jones.\'94 \
\'93C\'92mon boss, it will take me years to pay it off.\'94 Agent Jones was jubilant, if he was planning to dock his pay, he wasn\'92t planning to kill him. He was safe, at least for the immediate future. A cursory examination of the blast site, however, would quickly reveal, rather than the hole being blasted under the buildings, a tunnel had been dug. \
\'93The loss of the other agents was not unexpected and we must continue our mission.\'94 With only one agent left at his disposal, Hardman could do nothing else but ignore his suspicions until he had proof of treachery. He was under instructions to kill him at the conclusion of the operation and he would use him until then. \'93We are in the hands of our scientists at the moment, but while they are cooking up their potions, we can snatch a few Elvi off the street.\'94\
\'93Why don\'92t we just book a 5 or 6 piece Elvis show? I can arrange that if you want.\'94 Agent Jones confidently suggested.\
\'93That will save a whole heap of trouble. Go to it.\'94 Director Hardman was amused that Agent Jones had finally come up with a good idea.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::0>
\f5 * * *
\f0 \
\pard\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\pardeftab720\fi360\sl264\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f3\fs26 The Elvi war cabinet consisted of the High Elvis, his parliamentary cabinet plus the Blessed Mother, the Great Teacher, the Holy Aunts and Professor Hermann. The double agent, Agent Jones, reported to the war cabinet, when he was able, but was not permitted to opine on matters of policy. Meetings were scheduled for each morning at 6.00am and in the evenings at 6.00pm, when matters of urgency were debated and matters of strategy devised. The most urgent issue, of course, was the imminent threat from the PTD to the existence of the Elvi.\
\'93Why don\'92t we just infect all of the Elvi with the T-virus? They can throw what they like at us and it will not matter.\'94 The Minister for Health saw the issue, quite simplistically, as being a medical issue that would be resolved by inoculation.\
\'93That would not reduce the threat, just alter it. If they think we have immunity to their viral agent, then they will just change strategy. In any case there is not enough of the virus at hand to inoculate all 100,000 of us. We have to make them commit to the plan they have. Do we know when they are planning the abduction?\'94 The High Elvis was trying to think three moves ahead of the company agents he was up against. \
\'93How are we going to keep an eye on all of the Elvi?\'94 The Great Teacher could see, from the blank expressions before him, that the cupboard was bare on the other side of the table too. \
\'93Agent Jones made contact, High Elvis.\'94 Holy Aunt Hayley, police duties making her late as usual, drifted into the committee room holding her notepad and read the message. \'93He says, \'91Director Hardman will require a 6 piece Elvis band to play a gig at the Gravity Well Lounge, Penthouse Level Hardy Tower One. Thursday 25 June at 7.00pm.\'92 Agent Jones has, in effect, asked us to send in some sacrificial lambs. Now we decide who we offer up.\'94\
\'93We now have a crack team of operatives that could intercede.\'94 The Minister for Graceland Security proudly announced. \
\'93Director Hardman has arranged the gig in The Gravity Well for a reason. It\'92s deep in L.5. territory and the security is too tight. I guarantee they will be there in numbers and geared up for a slaughter. We will never be able to sneak in enough back-up to take them all. I do not think we have to intercede, in fact I suggest that we do nothing at all.\'94 As she spoke the faces of the cabinet became ashen, but as she continued the cabinet became stolid and unified with resolve. \'93They must have their lab rats to experiment on. I would therefore suggest we ready ourselves to innoculate with the T-virus, but only do so after we have our volunteers.\'94\
\'93Only you could think of such a plan, Detective.\'94 The Great Teacher added, memories of the Haloren Smythe arrest jumped to his mind.\
\'93Dispassionate would be an understatement.\'94 The High Elvis finally said after several minutes of silence. \'93You and Holy Aunt Kathy should be innoculated with the T-virus immediately.\'94\
\'93I already have the virus in my system, High Elvis.\'94 Holy Aunt Kathy knew the morning after The Great Teacher\'92s revival that something was very different. She had woken up energetic and clear headed, something she had not experienced since childhood. She had to stick three patches to her arm to make the strange feelings go away.\
\'93My team and I will have to get to work. Is there a suitable space available?\'94 Professor Hermann was keen to start manufacturing huge quantities of virus from the samples he had managed to grab on the way out of the bunker. \
\'93You and I have to be at the gig.\'94 Cracker whispered to Sarah. \'93I want to show you something. I can use my contacts to gain access, but you will have to arrange a booking for that night.\'94\
\'93A booking at the Gravity Well? That\'92s near impossible at such short notice, even for me!\'94 Sarah did not like sucking up to lowly receptionists at fashionable restaurants and she especially disliked feeling grateful if she managed to get a table on the night of her choice. \
\'93Yeah, well you are Eloise Shakti\'92s daughter-in-contract. Get her on the case.\'94 Cracker was not taking no for an answer. \'93Tell her you want to take Alex for a romantic dinner.\'94\
\'93A romantic dinner with Alex?\'94 She also did not like the idea of being seen in public with the husband. \'93Eloise would never believe it. I will have to come up with something better that that.\'94 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::0>
\f5 \uc0\u8232  * * *
\f0 \
\pard\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\pardeftab720\fi360\sl264\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f3\fs26 Three male and three female Elvi, dressed in their finest on-stage outfits of shiny gold suits with black lapels and matching reflective flares, were ready for their mission. Their glistening pitch black hair was combed directly upwards about 10 centimetres from the forehead into a bulbous, protuberant coiffure and slicked down over the crown and either side of their heads. The males had wide, bushy, but neat, sideburns that spread into black mutton-chops before tapering off to a point, just shy of the chin. They stood at attention before the war cabinet as the High Elvis stepped forward, ceremonially hugging and kissing each on both cheeks.\
\'93Each have you have volunteered for this mission and you are all aware of the dangers. If any of you want to reconsider, now is the time.\'94 The High Elvis waited for a few moments and was about to continued when he saw one of the volunteers lift his right foot to step forward.\
\'93Stand fast!\'94 The band leader, indistinguishable from the others, yelled loudly. The wavering foot of the volunteer was re-planted firmly back on the ground, heel wedged against heel. Proud to see his colleague back in line he called out, \'93Liberia Elvi superbia!\'94\
\'93Libera Elvi superbia!\'94 Replied the line with musical intonation and precision. \'93Libera Elvi superbia! Libera Elvi superbia!.\'94\
\'93Do you have the sample of the virus?\'94 The High Elvis asked of the band leader.\
\'93Yes, your highness.\'94 Band leader Elvis replied reverently. \'93Once we are inside their lab complex, we will release it.\'94\
\'93The location you release will be critical. Only you can make the decision, Elvis.\'94 Holy Aunt Hayley was very concerned the virus would be released too early and before it can deliver the results desired. \'93Ensure that at least one of their scientists is present, all of them preferably.\'94\
\'93Yes, Holy Aunt.\'94 His chest puffed out. \'93We will do our duty or die trying.\'94 They about faced and marched out of the committee room and were off to their gig. \
\'93Did you even tell them?\'94 The Great Teacher, like everyone else in the room was having second thoughts. \'93That it is a suicide mission?\'94\
\'93No, they will fight better if they don\'92t know.\'94 Holy Aunt Hayley countered. \
\'93For fuck\'92s sake. You could have got the same results if you sent me!\'94 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::0>
\f5 * * *
\f0 \
