\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f3\fs26 The kidnapped Elvi had been transferred to a brand new clandestine laboratory well outside the city limits. There were no roads to this facility and only a chosen few agency pilots were aware of it\'92s existence. Still unconscious they had been transferred to the testing chambers, all in a row, with no fuss. Each were strapped into an interrogation seat in the centre of a sealed chamber where they were to be subjected to multiple indignities and exposed to bio-agents of fiendish design. \
Agent Jones was the most experienced at enhanced interrogations and was the obvious choice to lead the interviews. Before they gave these Elvi their latest version of Ebola, the Director wanted to be certain that the Elvi were unaware of their plans. The chambers were massive cubes of ballistic rated poly-glass and the interrogations had attracted a great deal of morbid interest from those who had never had the chance to see a talented interrogator in action. Agent Jones unsealed the door of the first cube and entered, a small chefs roll in his right hand.\
\'93I know you!\'94 Drummer Elvis called out. \
\'93You will know me even better before the end of the day.\'94 Agent Jones smiled and looked around at his audience all filled with good humour and blood lust. He knew he had to be merciless with this Elvis and the other Elvi prisoners. He leaned in and whispered in the drummer\'92s right ear. \'93I am with you Elvis, I am here to ensure you play out your role. We have an audience, so I will have to make this look believable. You will be tortured and you will die, but I assure you the mission will be carried out. Do you understand?\'94 \
\'93I understand, thank you.\'94 The drummer said quietly. \'93The sample is in a small patch behind my ear.\'94\
\'93Thank you for delivering it to me. We have been in lock down for weeks. I am going to bite your ear off now.\'94 Agent Jones sank his teeth into the gristly flesh of the ear and tore at it until a sizable lump ripped free, along with a tiny plastic patch. The observers outside the cube erupted into applause as the Agent spat the ear into the air with theatrical flair. Initially, the crowd of scientists and sundry agents didn\'92t know why he was whispering in Elvis\'92 ear, but they had got their answer. The Elvis screamed, but he and the rest of his troupe knew they were on a one way mission and their fate mattered not.\
Agent Jones had at each Elvi with a clinical ferocity, maximising pain, but never endangering their lives. Every one of them, man and woman alike, kept to their story, that they were merely entertainers out to do a gig at the Gravity Well lounge. They all assured Agent Jones he had the wrong Elvis. They were pummeled into wads of bruised and bleeding flesh, but they never broke and Agent Jones admired them immensely. \
\'93They know nothing.\'94 Agent Jones offered up to the Director. \'93This lot are just singers and dancers.\'94\
\'93Good. We will commence testing in a few days, after they have rested up.\'94 Director Hardman was pleased. \'93I want them to die healthy.\'94 The operation seemed to being chugging along nicely and any suspicions about Agent Jones had evaporated when he spat out that first piece of Elvis ear. \
\'93How is the security on our samples?\'94 Agent Jones hoped he wasn\'92t too obvious.\
\'93I think we are all secure, but go and check if you wish.\'94 His suspicions about Agent Jones again leaped back into life. He hooked into the security feed and followed Agent Jones, by camera, down each corridor and through every check-point, until he had entered the storage facility. He saw him chat with the scientists, check a few things and then leave. He did not see him drop the tiny flat vial, down the inside of his trouser and onto the floor of main storage, nor did he notice him crush it underfoot. At the end of his shift, Agent Jones sleazed out of the facility, hitched a ride on an outgoing flight, hoping never to return.\
The following morning Director Hardman was in his office, waiting for the arrival of Agent Jones when the security alarm from the bio-lab began oscillating loudly. The holo-phone screamed, demanding some attention of it\'92s own and the disembodied head of the senior bio-engineer appeared above the emitter. \'93What\'92s up Dr?\'94\
\'93We have lost most of our samples.\'94 He let the terrible news settle before carrying on. \'93Every sample in main storage has died. I don\'92t know how, but the entire lab has a pleasant lemony fresh scent.\'94\
\'93Sounds like sabotage to me.\'94 The Director was certain. 
\f4\i Where the hell is Jones.
\f3\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

