\f3\fs26 \'93How did this happen?\'94 Director Hardman screamed at Professor ???\
\'93We have been the victim of a biological attack, but of a most benign kind.\'94 Prof ???\
\'93Benign?\'94 The Director was incredulous. \'93The operation is in ruins.\'94\
\'93Sir, I have a sample of the organism used. It only attacks human pathogens, but in the external environment. It does not tolerate heat above 35 degrees and cannot survive inside the human body. It was released on the floor of main storage and then it spread out across the floor and transferred by foot traffic everywhere, including inside the cool room and the entire inventory stored there was destroyed. They wanted to kill our pathogens, Mr Director, not us.\'94\
\'93Benign, huh? Anything else?\'94\
\'93Not all of our inventory was in the cool room. Dr Stroman was working on a promising variety of a synthetic bio-agent in his lab last night. His lab has been quarantined until we clear the facility of the contaminant.\'94\
\'93How much of a setback is it then?\'94\
\'93All not lost. It may take a month to get back to speed, but Stroman thinks he is close to a breakthrough.\'94\
\'93I want testing to commence on the Elvi within two weeks.\'94\
