\f3\fs26 \'93Agent Jones, the Elvi nation owes you a debt of gratitude. You have served us well and will hereby be known as the Great Protector.\'94 The Parliament erupted in applause, stomping their feet so hard the plaster ceiling began to crumble. The High Elvis raised his right hand and the cacophony ceased. \
\'93This Parliament is in recess.\'94 The speaker of the house banged his gavel and the representatives shuffled out.\
\'93Great Protector, I expect to see you at the War Cabinet meeting this evening.\'94 The High Elvis said over his shoulder as he left the chamber.\
\'93Yes, sir.\'94 Agent Jones did not feel like much of a protector, certainly not a great one.\

